{
  "_comment": [
    "Per-hostname multi-engine gate for Ralph Orchestrator.",
    "Copy this file to engines-config.json (remove the .example suffix) to enable.",
    "",
    "How it works:",
    "  On startup, orchestrator.sh reads this file and looks up the current machine's",
    "  hostname (from `hostname` command). If found under 'hosts', that machine's",
    "  settings override the RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE env var. If not found, 'default' is used.",
    "  If this file is absent, RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE defaults to false (Claude-only mode).",
    "",
    "Authentication requirements when RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE=true:",
    "  - Codex: run `codex login` to authenticate with your OpenAI account.",
    "           Config stored in ~/.codex/config.toml",
    "  - Gemini: run `gemini login` (or use GEMINI_API_KEY env var) for Google auth.",
    "           Assumes headed environment (browser-based OAuth).",
    "  - Claude: existing ~/.claude/.credentials.json used as before.",
    "",
    "Removing this comment block: the '_comment' key is ignored by the loader."
  ],
  "default": {
    "RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE": false
  },
  "hosts": {
    "my-codex-machine": {
      "RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE": true
    },
    "dev-workstation": {
      "RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE": true
    },
    "ci-runner": {
      "RALPH_MULTI_ENGINE": false
    }
  }
}
